  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the Reintegration of Men and Women Formerly Associated with Non-state Armed Groups Through Social Cohesion Activities During Rehabilitation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building upon the success of the pilot and recognising the importance of these social cohesion activities to the reintegration process, this project offers a model of ongoing social cohesion that promotes the connection between male disengaged combatants and women formerly associated with non-state armed groups, with community members throughout the reintegration process.</narrative>
  </description>
